  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieved 0.591 acc, a large jump over config_001 (singleprofile, 0.485), confirming multiprofile aggregation is highly beneficial. Image-only is very weak (0.208), so RNA is the dominant signal. Uncertainty: we don't yet know whether transformer aggregation can further improve over avgpool for the multiprofile RNA setting. This experiment (config_003) changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding rna_only, multiprofile, and pca_n2000 fixed, giving a clean single-variable comparison against the current best. If transformer helps, it establishes a stronger aggregation baseline before introducing new encoders or multimodal fusion; if it doesn't, avgpool is confirmed as sufficient and we can pivot to encoder exploration. With 6 experiments remaining after this, isolating the best aggregation for the proven multiprofile-RNA setup is the highest-information next step."
}

